{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Review use of synthetic hormones in hormone replacement therapy",
        "additional_details": "We want an independent review of synthetic use of HRT across England, including testosterone uses, and what we see as a 'one size fits all' approach. There must be interventions where improvement is inadequate. Women across England deserve consistent, personalised, identical replacement, evidence-based and National standards must be enforceable, and publicly monitored, with clear responsibility at every level of the NHS.",
        "background": "We call on the Government to review menopause and hormone replacement therapy (HRT) care across England, particularly the approach to cases where hormone treatments are failing to improve symptoms.",
